    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0470" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/78</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dickover</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2101</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-27">October 27,
                        1936</date>.<lb/>[Received November 16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 1753, March 30, 1936,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d301-f1"/> in regard to
                    a rumored German-Japanese military agreement and to enclose herewith a
                    memorandum of conversation which I had on October 26, with Baron de
                    Bassompierre, the Belgian Ambassador in Tokyo. The Ambassador’s opinion is that
                    there is some truth in the rumors of this agreement, which he believes is now
                    approaching some definite form.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dickover</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d301-a1.xml" xpointer="d301-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
